{{Short description|Use of IT or ICT in the travel industry}}
{{More citations needed|date=November 2007}}
'''Travel technology''' (also called '''tourism technology''', and '''hospitality automation''') is the application of [[Information Technology]] (IT) or [[Information and Communications Technology]] (ICT) in the [[travel]], [[tourism]] and [[hospitality industry]]. Some forms of travel technology are [[Tracking (commercial airline flight)|flight tracking]], pre-travel planning through online travel agencies, and systems that allow tourists to review their experiences.

Travel technology was originally associated with the [[computer reservations system]] (CRS) of the airline industry, but is now used more inclusively, incorporating the broader tourism sector as well as its subset the hospitality industry.

